      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet in the heart of the breathtaking coastal area of Dooks, Glenbeigh, this exceptional detached residence presents a rare opportunity to acquire a spacious and beautifully designed family home in one of County Kerry's most scenic and sought-after seaside locations. Extending to just under 2,300 sq. ft. and occupying a generous site of approximately half an acre, the property enjoys stunning views across the nearby beach, the Atlantic coastline, and the surrounding natural landscape, offering a truly unique coastal lifestyle.\nFrom the moment you arrive, the property immediately impresses with its striking design, peaceful setting, and seamless connection to the outdoors. The home has been thoughtfully planned to maximise natural light, space, and comfort, while perfectly complementing its spectacular surroundings. Every aspect of the layout has been carefully considered to suit modern family living, combining open-plan spaces with cosy retreats and private accommodation.\nUpon entering the home, you are welcomed into a magnificent open-plan kitchen and dining area that undoubtedly serves as the heart of the property. This remarkable room is enhanced by dramatic double-height vaulted ceilings, creating an incredible sense of openness and light throughout the space. The focal point of this area is an impressive central stone clad chimney with a double sided wood burner. Large windows and glazed sections frame the coastal views while flooding the interior with natural daylight, further enhancing the bright and airy atmosphere. The kitchen and dining area provides an ideal setting for family gatherings, entertaining guests, or simply relaxing while enjoying the ever-changing scenery outside.\nAdjacent to the kitchen lies a warm and inviting living room which overlooks the rear garden and enjoys beautiful sea views. This elegant yet comfortable space offers the perfect retreat to relax and unwind in every season, with the surrounding coastal environment providing a constant backdrop of tranquillity. Just off the kitchen, there is also a cosy den which offers excellent flexibility and could serve as a snug, reading room, home office, or informal lounge area depending on individual requirements.\nThe ground floor accommodation continues with four generously proportioned bedrooms one of which is ensuite, each offering comfortable and versatile living space suitable for family members or visiting guests. A well-appointed family bathroom serves this section of the home, while a practical utility room provides valuable additional storage and everyday convenience.\nUpstairs, a superb games room occupies its own private retreat away from the main living accommodation. Exceptionally spacious and beautifully presented, this versatile space provides the perfect setting for relaxation, entertainment, and family enjoyment. Benefiting from an elevated position, the room enjoys a peaceful atmosphere that complements the home's coastal setting, while the surrounding scenery can be appreciated from the comfort of this inviting upper-level haven.\nExternally, the property is equally appealing. To the front, there is ample private parking for multiple vehicles, ensuring practicality for both homeowners and visitors alike. The large rear garden offers an abundance of outdoor space ideal for children, gardening enthusiasts, or outdoor entertaining during the warmer months. Mature surroundings and open lawns combine to create a wonderful extension of the home's living space.\nWithout question, one of the most exceptional features of this remarkable property is the direct access to the beach from the rear garden. This truly rare attribute allows residents to step directly onto the sand and enjoy the beauty of the shoreline within moments. Whether for swimming, walking, water sports, or simply enjoying the peaceful coastal setting, this unique connection to the beach makes the property an extraordinary home in the highly desirable Dooks area of Glenbeigh.\n\nDooks, Glenbeigh is one of Kerry's most picturesque coastal locations, renowned for its stunning beaches and breathtaking scenery along the Wild Atlantic Way. The renowned Dooks Golf Course is a 10 minute walk down the beach or a few minutes drive. There are also many other impressive golf courses in the County, such as Waterville, Ballybunion, Tralee and Killarney to name a few. While offering a peaceful and relaxed seaside lifestyle, the area also enjoys excellent connectivity to nearby towns and amenities. The vibrant town of Killorglin is approximately 10 minutes away, while Killarney can be reached in under 40 minutes, providing a wide range of shops, restaurants, schools, and leisure facilities. Kerry Airport is conveniently located within an hour's drive, offering regular domestic and international flights, while Cork and Shannon Airports are both easily accessible for further travel connections. The nearby villages of Glenbeigh and Cahersiveen also provide a charming selection of cafés, pubs, and local services, making Dooks an ideal location for both permanent living and holiday retreats."
